sourcing doesn’t always work#{1}":[526,530]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Audrey Dutton","target":"Audrey Dutton","line":5},{"title":"Watchdog","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/local/investigations/watchdog/","line":16},{"title":"Idaho highway contractors changed records hundreds of times. Then, they got bonuses","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/odpjfs/picture240518291/alternates/LANDSCAPE_1200/0223%20aspalt%20illustration.jpg","line":34,"embedded":true},{"title":"Idaho highway contractors changed records hundreds of times. Then, they got bonuses","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/local/investigations/watchdog/article239690033.html","line":38},{"title":"Back in 2002, he spoke up about falsifying Idaho road-construction tests. What happened?","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/e8avzw/picture240228766/alternates/LANDSCAPE_1200/BOI_02xxidtmeridiankunabend","line":40,"embedded":true},{"title":"Back in 2002, he spoke up about falsifying Idaho road-construction tests. What happened?","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/local/investigations/watchdog/article240540731.html","line":44},{"title":"Privatization or piratization: Idaho learns again that outsourcing doesn’t always work","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/odpjfs/picture240518291/alternates/LANDSCAPE_1200/0223%20aspalt%20illustration.jpg","line":46,"embedded":true},{"title":"Privatization or piratization: Idaho learns again that outsourcing doesn’t always work","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/opinion/editorials/article240697256.html","line":50},{"title":"facing a projected $3.6 billion shortfall over the next 20 years","target":"https://www.infrastructurereportcard.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/FullReport-Idaho.pdf","line":80},{"title":"a budget that includes$488 million for road construction","target":"https://legislature.idaho.gov/wp-content/uploads/budget/publications/Legislative-Budget-Book/2020/Legislative%20Budget%20Book.pdf","line":82},{"title":"“business-friendly” when it comes to oversight","target":"https://commerce.idaho.gov/business-climate/","line":84},{"title":"Gov. Brad Little seeks to reduce government regulation","target":"https://gov.idaho.gov/pressrelease/idaho-cuts-and-simplifies-75-percent-of-rules-in-one-year-becomes-least-regulated-state-in-country/","line":84},{"title":"Traffic along Meridian Road (ID-69) between turns toward downtown Kuna. A road construction project here from 2018 was identified as having “suspicious alterations” in its asphalt test results.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/e8avzw/picture240228766/alternates/FREE_1200/BOI_02xxidtmeridiankunabend","line":94,"embedded":true},{"title":"Idaho statute says","target":"https://legislature.idaho.gov/statutesrules/idstat/title74/t74ch1/sect74-102/","line":138},{"title":"adutton@idahostatesman.com","target":"mailto:adutton@idahostatesman.com","line":158},{"title":"Idaho Gov. Brad Little","target":"mailto:governor@gov.idaho.gov","line":164},{"title":"Brian Ness, director of Idaho Transportation Department","target":"mailto:brian.ness@itd.idaho.gov","line":166},{"title":"Scott Bedke, Idaho Speaker of the House","target":"mailto:SBedke@house.idaho.gov","line":168},{"title":"Brent Hill, Idaho Senate President Pro Tem","target":"mailto:bhill@senate.idaho.gov","line":170},{"title":"**subscribe to the Statesman today.**","target":"https://account.idahostatesman.com/subscribe/create?param=fHpHCEc=&offer=NmEfaxcUb3lSCUJAfRIoaTBECgE2CzAqAQFDG15QPgoUG0hQeHNDAEJKb29STx0HLisVS1BIbwE%2FcEtLfA4%2FGw8%3D&cid=soc_employee-cta-adutton-asphaltinvestigation_201901","line":176},{"title":"91% of Idaho’s pavements are in good or fair condition, exceeding the state’s goal of 80%","target":"https://apps.itd.idaho.gov/Apps/ScorecardDMZ/Home/NETDetailView/139","line":246},{"title":"Moderate distress usually means cracks of various types, but it can mean other issues like potholes","target":"https://www.fhwa.dot.gov/publications/research/infrastructure/pavements/ltpp/13092/13092.pdf","line":256},{"title":"A semi-truck heads down US-95 at Lewiston Hill. The Federal Highway Administration sent a team to look at Idaho roads in 2017, after Idaho Transportation Department staff contacted the agency with concerns about asphalt testing. The FHWA team told ITD that the North Idaho highway already showed “moderate distress” two years after being repaved.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/6f8oz3/picture240542881/alternates/FREE_1200/Lewiston%20Hill","line":258,"embedded":true},{"title":"ITD wrote in 2015","target":"https://apps.itd.idaho.gov/apps/MediaManagerMVC/transporter/2015/022715_Trans/022715_US95PavingAward.html","line":266},{"title":"found it takes an average of 22 to 28 years for asphalt roads to show moderate distress","target":"http://www.asphaltroads.org/assets/_control/content/files/IM024_LTPP_Report.pdf","line":268},{"title":"The Idaho Statesman reviewed records from a road project on Meridian Road between Kuna and Meridian, including this log of changes to one asphalt test result. The state, whose job is to verify that contractors are putting high-quality asphalt on Idaho’s roads, had hired a company to perform this test on its behalf. The state paid the contractor more than $2 million for asphalt on the project.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/5owqrm/picture240544986/alternates/FREE_1200/Asphalt%20test%20graphic","line":278,"embedded":true},{"title":"mentioned in a recent meeting of the Ada County Highway District, describing it as an attempt at “hacking” by ITD","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/local/community/boise/article240440986.html","line":290},{"title":"investigation echoes an inquiry in 2002","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/local/investigations/watchdog/article240540731.html","line":314},{"title":"Growth around Kuna has attracted an increase in business development along Meridian Road near Deer Flat Road.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/fe1p5p/picture240228736/alternates/FREE_1200/BOI_02xxidtmeridianrdabove","line":336,"embedded":true},{"title":"Deb Mishra, who now works for Oklahoma State University","target":"https://cive.okstate.edu/node/221","line":356},{"title":"In 2018, Idaho received about $301 million in federal highway funds","target":"https://fas.org/sgp/crs/misc/R45727.pdf","line":410},{"title":"adutton@idahostatesman.com","target":"mailto:adutton@idahostatesman.com","line":450},{"title":"Idaho Gov. Brad Little","target":"mailto:governor@gov.idaho.gov","line":456},{"title":"Brian Ness, director of Idaho Transportation Department","target":"mailto:brian.ness@itd.idaho.gov","line":458},{"title":"Scott Bedke, Idaho Speaker of the House","target":"mailto:SBedke@house.idaho.gov","line":460},{"title":"Brent Hill, Idaho Senate President Pro Tem","target":"mailto:bhill@senate.idaho.gov","line":462},{"title":"![Profile Image of Audrey Dutton","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/a8j3oe/picture221753160/alternates/FREE_1200/AudreyDutton-profile.jpg","line":484},{"title":"Audrey Dutton","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/profile/218245750/","line":486},{"title":"208-377-6448","target":"tel:208-377-6448","line":490},{"title":"CLAIM OFFER","target":"https://mycheckout.idahostatesman.com/subscribe?ofrgp_id=428&g2i_or_o=OnSite&g2i_or_p=CTA&cid=cta_dynamic-zone_3a_default-1-1mo-15.99_202305","line":496},{"title":"Idaho highway contractors changed records hundreds of times. Then, they got bonuses","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/odpjfs/picture240518291/alternates/LANDSCAPE_1200/0223%20aspalt%20illustration.jpg","line":504,"embedded":true},{"title":"Back in 2002, he spoke up about falsifying Idaho road-construction tests. What happened?","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/e8avzw/picture240228766/alternate