"smart_blocks:2020-02-22 - Idaho highway contractors changed records hundreds of times. Then, they got bonuses (1).md##READ MORE#Are Idaho’s roads safe and sound?": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"10ci275","at":1785795016021},"key":"2020-02-22 - Idaho highway contractors changed records hundreds of times. Then, they got bonuses (1).md##READ MORE#Are Idaho’s roads safe and sound?","lines":[250,311],"size":7344,"outlinks":[{"title":"Moderate distress usually means cracks of various types, but it can mean other issues like potholes","target":"https://www.fhwa.dot.gov/publications/research/infrastructure/pavements/ltpp/13092/13092.pdf","line":7},{"title":"A semi-truck heads down US-95 at Lewiston Hill. The Federal Highway Administration sent a team to look at Idaho roads in 2017, after Idaho Transportation Department staff contacted the agency with concerns about asphalt testing. The FHWA team told ITD that the North Idaho highway already showed “moderate distress” two years after being repaved.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/6f8oz3/picture240542881/alternates/FREE_1200/Lewiston%20Hill","line":9,"embedded":true},{"title":"ITD wrote in 2015","target":"https://apps.itd.idaho.gov/apps/MediaManagerMVC/transporter/2015/022715_Trans/022715_US95PavingAward.html","line":17},{"title":"found it takes an average of 22 to 28 years for asphalt roads to show moderate distress","target":"http://www.asphaltroads.org/assets/_control/content/files/IM024_LTPP_Report.pdf","line":19},{"title":"The Idaho Statesman reviewed records from a road project on Meridian Road between Kuna and Meridian, including this log of changes to one asphalt test result. The state, whose job is to verify that contractors are putting high-quality asphalt on Idaho’s roads, had hired a company to perform this test on its behalf. The state paid the contractor more than $2 million for asphalt on the project.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/5owqrm/picture240544986/alternates/FREE_1200/Asphalt%20test%20graphic","line":29,"embedded":true},{"title":"mentioned in a recent meeting of the Ada County Highway District, describing it as an attempt at “hacking” by ITD","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/local/community/boise/article240440986.html","line":41}],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
"smart_blocks:2020-02-22 - Idaho highway contractors changed records hundreds of times. Then, they got bonuses (1).md##READ MORE#Are Idaho’s roads safe and sound?#{1}": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"irs4yi","at":1785795016021},"key":"2020-02-22 - Idaho highway contractors changed records hundreds of times. Then, they got bonuses (1).md##READ MORE#Are Idaho’s roads safe and sound?#{1}","lines":[252,311],"size":7305,"outlinks":[{"title":"Moderate distress usually means cracks of various types, but it can mean other issues like potholes","target":"https://www.fhwa.dot.gov/publications/research/infrastructure/pavements/ltpp/13092/13092.pdf","line":5},{"title":"A semi-truck heads down US-95 at Lewiston Hill. The Federal Highway Administration sent a team to look at Idaho roads in 2017, after Idaho Transportation Department staff contacted the agency with concerns about asphalt testing. The FHWA team told ITD that the North Idaho highway already showed “moderate distress” two years after being repaved.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/6f8oz3/picture240542881/alternates/FREE_1200/Lewiston%20Hill","line":7,"embedded":true},{"title":"ITD wrote in 2015","target":"https://apps.itd.idaho.gov/apps/MediaManagerMVC/transporter/2015/022715_Trans/022715_US95PavingAward.html","line":15},{"title":"found it takes an average of 22 to 28 years for asphalt roads to show moderate distress","target":"http://www.asphaltroads.org/assets/_control/content/files/IM024_LTPP_Report.pdf","line":17},{"title":"The Idaho Statesman reviewed records from a road project on Meridian Road between Kuna and Meridian, including this log of changes to one asphalt test result. The state, whose job is to verify that contractors are putting high-quality asphalt on Idaho’s roads, had hired a company to perform this test on its behalf. The state paid the contractor more than $2 million for asphalt on the project.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/5owqrm/picture240544986/alternates/FREE_1200/Asphalt%20test%20graphic","line":27,"embedded":true},{"title":"mentioned in a recent meeting of the Ada County Highway District, describing it as an attempt at “hacking” by ITD","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/local/community/boise/article240440986.html","line":39}],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
